    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule: the response flags `true` when more than 80 owners have already been created today, otherwise `false`.\n\nKeeping structural impact low, I avoided touching the large `Owner` entity (and the `schema.sql` DDL that a persisted column would require). Instead the flag is derived at response time and set on the DTO. Three files changed plus one tiny new helper:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (generates `OwnerDto.setBulkSignupWarning`).\n- **`BulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 a small cohesive helper (`WMC_other = 0`, CC = 1) counting owners whose `registrationDate` is today's business day and returning `count > 80`, reusing the existing `BusinessDay` roll used by the daily-limit rule.\n- **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder) and **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder) \u2014 each maps to the DTO, then sets `bulkSignupWarning` via `BulkSignup.warns(...)`. Both are near-empty classes, so the surrounding-complexity cost is minimal.\n\nNo mapper change was needed (the DTO field is set explicitly after mapping; MapStruct's default unmapped policy is WARN, not ERROR). `AcceptanceTest` and the full build pass.",
